<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<title>Manual Ilustrado Hospedagem e DNS CONAE</title>
</head>
<body style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 24px;">
  <h1 style="color: #064e3b; text-align: center;">CONAE — Manual Visual Passo a Passo: Hospedagem, Link Fixo e DNS com Firebase</h1>
  <p style="text-align: center; color: #4b5563;">Projeto Firebase: <strong>dazzling-decorator-x01dl</strong> · Banco Firestore: <strong>ai-studio-2df24a12-52ee-49c2-b341-b1026e2bf9a0</strong></p>
  
    <div style="page-break-after: always; margin-bottom: 24px;">
      <h2 style="color: #064e3b; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; border-bottom: 2px solid #d97706; padding-bottom: 6px;">Visao Geral — Hospedagem, Link Fixo e DNS com Firebase</h2>
      <p style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; color: #1f2937; line-height: 1.5;">O Google Drive nao hospeda aplicativos web (apenas guarda arquivos). Use GitHub + Vercel/Cloudflare Pages (100% pelo navegador) ou Firebase Hosting no seu projeto dazzling-decorator-x01dl.</p>
      <p style="text-align: center;">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="660" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 2px solid #d97706;" />
      </p>
    </div>
  

    <div style="page-break-after: always; margin-bottom: 24px;">
      <h2 style="color: #064e3b; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; border-bottom: 2px solid #d97706; padding-bottom: 6px;">Passo 1 e 2 — Exportar para o GitHub e Publicar na Vercel (Gratis)</h2>
      <p style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; color: #1f2937; line-height: 1.5;">1) Salve/exporte o projeto no GitHub (ex: conae-app). 2) Acesse vercel.com, entre com GitHub, clique em Add New -> Project, importe conae-app e clique em Deploy para ganhar seu link fixo HTTPS.</p>
      <p style="text-align: center;">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="660" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 2px solid #d97706;" />
      </p>
    </div>
  

    <div style="page-break-after: always; margin-bottom: 24px;">
      <h2 style="color: #064e3b; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; border-bottom: 2px solid #d97706; padding-bottom: 6px;">Passo 3 — Conectar seu Dominio Proprio (DNS)</h2>
      <p style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; color: #1f2937; line-height: 1.5;">Na Vercel (Settings -> Domains), adicione seu dominio (ex: seusite.com.br). Copie os registros Tipo A (@ -> 76.76.21.21) e CNAME (www -> cname.vercel-dns.com) para o painel DNS do Registro.br, Cloudflare ou Hostinger.</p>
      <p style="text-align: center;">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="660" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 2px solid #d97706;" />
      </p>
    </div>
  

    <div style="page-break-after: always; margin-bottom: 24px;">
      <h2 style="color: #064e3b; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; border-bottom: 2px solid #d97706; padding-bottom: 6px;">Passo 4 (Obrigatorio) — Liberar o Novo Link no Firebase</h2>
      <p style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; color: #1f2937; line-height: 1.5;">Abra o Firebase Console (projeto dazzling-decorator-x01dl) -> Authentication -> Settings -> Dominios autorizados -> Adicionar dominio. Digite o link novo (ex: conae-app.vercel.app e seusite.com.br). Seu banco Firestore continua 100% conectado sem perder nenhum dado.</p>
      <p style="text-align: center;">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="660" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 2px solid #d97706;" />
      </p>
    </div>
  

    <div style="page-break-after: auto; margin-bottom: 24px;">
      <h2 style="color: #064e3b; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; border-bottom: 2px solid #d97706; padding-bottom: 6px;">Opcao Alternativa — Hospedar Direto no Firebase Hosting</h2>
      <p style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt; color: #1f2937; line-height: 1.5;">Seu projeto ja tem firebase.json e .firebaserc configurados. No computador rode: npm install -g firebase-tools, firebase login e npm run deploy:hosting. Depois conecte seu dominio em Hosting -> Adicionar dominio personalizado.</p>
      <p style="text-align: center;">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="660" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 2px solid #d97706;" />
      </p>
    </div>
  
</body>
</html>